    <string name="sep_title">Vocal and backing-track separation</string>
    <string name="sep_intro">A track is split into two files: vocals and instrumental (backing track). They stay in the app, and any result can be sent to RVC conversion with one tap. The model is loaded only while it works and unloaded afterwards.</string>
    <string name="sep_model">Model</string>
    <string name="sep_model_missing">%1$s (missing)</string>
    <string name="sep_model_hint">Voc FT isolates vocals the cleanest. Kim Vocal 2 is the backup: it sometimes preserves quiet instruments better. Both are MDX-Net models from Ultimate Vocal Remover, offline, ~67 MB.</string>
    <string name="sep_lowmem_t">Save memory</string>
    <string name="sep_lowmem_h">Lower peak RAM, slightly slower. Keep it on for weak devices.</string>
    <string name="sep_smooth_t">Smooth seams</string>
    <string name="sep_smooth_h">Pieces of the track are joined with an overlap: no clicks, about 20 percent longer.</string>
    <string name="sep_denoise_t">Denoise the result</string>
    <string name="sep_denoise_h">The model runs twice: slightly cleaner, but twice as slow.</string>
    <string name="sep_pick">Choose a track</string>
    <string name="sep_go">Split</string>
    <string name="sep_heavy">Separation is the heaviest operation: the track is processed in ~6 s pieces, which takes a noticeable time on a phone. You can turn the screen off: it keeps working in the background with a notification.</string>
    <string name="sep_list_title">Separated songs</string>
